.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was written on 2026-09-26: the platform built thirty goldens of its own and
had no way to make one like them plus a script.
.Pp
On 2026-09-29, writing this page: run as a user,
.Nm
re-executed itself with the name alone, having already consumed its
options, so every such run failed with
.Dq --from is required ;
it cloned a base's current disk rather than its sealed snapshot; a failed
script exited with the script's code; and a failed
.Fl -ram
was ignored.
Building from a golden made by
.Nm
also found that
.Xr kvm-clone 8
gave a clone of a clone its source's identity.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The guest has network access while the scripts run, as the base gives it;
a script that downloads is only as offline as its sources.
.Pp
The guest's host key is not checked: every clone has a new one.
.Pp
.Fl -ram
and
.Fl -cpus
are set on the machine being built; machines cloned from the golden copy
them, and can be changed each with
.Xr virsh 1 .
